WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.336 --> 00:00:18.250
The school nurse called Patrick's mom to pick him up from school.

2
00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:22.993
Back at home Patrick climbed into bed and slept until late the next morning.

3
00:00:22.994 --> 00:00:29.749
"That's one good thing about getting a stomach bug," he thought. "Now I have the weekend to study for my math test!"

4
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:38.400
And he had Slider to keep him company. The cat curled up near his feet, purring contentedly as Patrick studied.

5
00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:45.742
Two hours later Patrick's phone chirped. He had a text from Dell: Feel up to some catch?

6
00:00:45.743 --> 00:00:54.056
Patrick stared at the words for a second. Then he started typing. Why did you tell Coach about my math test?

7
00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:59.216
Wasn't me! Probably your math teacher told him?

8
00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:04.311
"Oh," Patrick said out loud. That made sense. Of course.

9
00:01:04.312 --> 00:01:08.306
The teachers were supposed to inform Coach if an athlete was struggling.

10
00:01:08.307 --> 00:01:12.869
Patrick instantly felt bad about accusing his teammate. This was Dell.

11
00:01:12.871 --> 00:01:16.790
And Dell would never tell Coach about Patrick's math problems.

12
00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:22.369
He typed his reply: At the park in 15.

13
00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:28.792
Dell was locking up his bike when Patrick arrived.

14
00:01:28.793 --> 00:01:33.481
They warmed up for a while, tossing the ball back and forth.

15
00:01:33.481 --> 00:01:37.776
"Coach was worried when you didn't show up for practice yesterday," said Dell.

16
00:01:37.777 --> 00:01:41.933
"I told him you had gone home sick and that we'd work together over the weekend."

17
00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.698
He stopped his windup and looked at Patrick.

18
00:01:44.699 --> 00:01:51.197
"You don't mind practicing today, do you? With the big game against the Hornets coming up, I figured—"

19
00:01:51.198 --> 00:01:55.838
"Of course I don't mind!" Patrick grinned at him. "Let's get busy."

20
00:01:55.839 --> 00:02:01.013
Patrick relaxed as the ball whizzed into his glove over and over.

21
00:02:01.014 --> 00:02:04.830
It felt great to be playing baseball, catching with Dell.

22
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:08.501
But he still didn't feel ready to face the rest of the team yet.

23
00:02:08.502 --> 00:02:12.998
He'd acted like a jerk the other day and assumed everyone was laughing at him.

24
00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.570
He'd also been making a lot of mistakes on the field lately.

25
00:02:16.571 --> 00:02:22.071
By now he was sure everyone liked Mickey a whole lot more than they liked him.

26
00:02:22.072 --> 00:02:25.912
Around dinnertime Daniel opened Patrick's bedroom door.

27
00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:32.049
"Dad said he'd drop us off at Mickey's for a team pizza party. Be ready in a half hour."

28
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:38.882
"A team pizza party?" Patrick stared down at his math book. "Uh . . . I'm not going."

29
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:43.720
"What?" Daniel stepped into the room.

30
00:02:43.721 --> 00:02:50.957
"Dude, it's a team party. It's like a pep rally, a bonding thing for the whole team before the big game against the Hornets."

31
00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:53.801
"I'm still sick," Patrick lied.

32
00:02:53.802 --> 00:02:57.130
Daniel gave him a look. "No, you're not."

33
00:02:57.131 --> 00:03:04.369
"Anyway, Mickey is everybody's favorite new player," Patrick blurted out. "Nobody will miss me."

34
00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:09.128
He lifted Daniel's old mitt, which was lying on the floor next to his bed.

35
00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:13.862
"You can take this mitt back. I think the magic's gone."

36
00:03:13.863 --> 00:03:23.284
Daniel took the mitt and slipped his hand inside. "It's not magic, Patrick. It's just another dumb baseball superstition.

37
00:03:23.285 --> 00:03:28.530
But you don't need magic or superstitions. I have confidence in you."

38
00:03:28.531 --> 00:03:33.775
Patrick blinked in surprise. "Then why do you criticize everything I do?"

39
00:03:33.776 --> 00:03:37.760
Daniel shrugged. "I guess I am a little tough on you."

40
00:03:37.761 --> 00:03:42.337
"A little tough?" Patrick echoed. "You're brutal!

41
00:03:42.338 --> 00:03:50.664
When Dell and I didn't pick off that base runner, you made a really big deal of it—in front of the whole team. I felt like an idiot."

42
00:03:50.665 --> 00:03:56.496
"Look, this is my first coaching job. I want to do a good job for Coach.

43
00:03:56.497 --> 00:04:02.485
Plus, I've been pushing you hard because I wanted you to get the starter position—and keep it."

44
00:04:02.486 --> 00:04:05.065
"Well, I lost it."

45
00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:08.318
"I'm sorry for being hard on you," Daniel went on.

46
00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:11.056
"And who knows how the rest of the season will go.

47
00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:15.230
My guess is that sometimes you'll catch, and sometimes Mickey will catch.

48
00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:19.386
But tonight isn't about you or me. It's about the team."

49
00:04:19.387 --> 00:04:26.647
He tossed the mitt onto the bed. "The mitt is yours. And you should go to the pizza party.

50
00:04:26.648 --> 00:04:30.722
That's what team players do—they support their team."

51
00:04:30.723 --> 00:04:39.628
"Okay," Patrick mumbled. He hung his head as he headed for the shower a minute later.

52
00:04:39.629 --> 00:04:41.926
"Daniel's right," he thought.

53
00:04:41.927 --> 00:04:46.445
Patrick had been thinking about himself—instead of his team.

54
00:04:46.446 --> 00:04:49.711
"Thanks for the ride, Dad," said Daniel.

55
00:04:49.712 --> 00:04:56.528
"Yeah," said Patrick. "I'm glad you drove us in your car. It's embarrassing to ride around in Mom's van."

56
00:04:56.529 --> 00:05:02.620
Mr. Deboe laughed. "That van isn't too comfortable either.

57
00:05:02.621 --> 00:05:05.179
But it's good advertising for your mom.

58
00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:12.742
She's wanted to start this business for a long time, and taking the van to games and practices is a small way we can support her."

59
00:05:12.743 --> 00:05:16.429
"It's like taking one for the team," said Daniel.

60
00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.831
"Exactly," said Mr. Deboe.

61
00:05:19.832 --> 00:05:26.743
Patrick felt horrible. He'd been so embarrassed about the van, he hadn't thought about Mom for one second.

62
00:05:26.744 --> 00:05:30.917
Of course, she attracted new clients with that crazy van.

63
00:05:30.918 --> 00:05:34.998
It was definitely time for him to stop feeling sorry for himself.

64
00:05:34.999 --> 00:05:42.838
"Woof!" he said as he climbed out of the car. "Team Deboe is on the go!"

65
00:05:42.839 --> 00:05:46.136
"That's the spirit!" said his father.

66
00:05:46.137 --> 00:05:53.174
When Mickey saw Daniel and Patrick approaching the house, he flung open the front door.

67
00:05:53.175 --> 00:05:58.144
"Hey, guys!" He looked at Patrick. "I wasn't sure you were coming."

68
00:05:58.145 --> 00:06:01.245
"Stomach flu," mumbled Patrick.

69
00:06:01.246 --> 00:06:05.230
"The Deboes are here!" Mickey called to the rest of the team.

70
00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:11.726
"We've got one assistant coach and a survivor of the cafeteria's 'Friday Special!'"

71
00:06:11.727 --> 00:06:18.940
He raised Patrick's hand like a boxer as some kids cheered.

72
00:06:18.941 --> 00:06:22.058
"I barely survived," joked Patrick.

73
00:06:22.059 --> 00:06:26.542
"Yeah, the cafeteria food is horrible in middle school," said Buck.

74
00:06:26.543 --> 00:06:32.410
Daniel went to get some pizza while Patrick stood awkwardly with Mickey.

75
00:06:32.411 --> 00:06:36.047
"Where's your dog?" he asked, trying to make conversation.

76
00:06:36.048 --> 00:06:41.789
"Ratty's outside, showing off." Mickey pulled back a window curtain.

77
00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:50.012
Patrick saw Todd throwing a ball for the dog to fetch. "Looks like Ratty's found a friend."

78
00:06:50.013 --> 00:06:55.036
"Ratty's been lonesome since my brother left for college. I'm more of a cat person."

79
00:06:55.037 --> 00:06:58.661
"Really? You like cats?" said Patrick.

80
00:06:58.662 --> 00:07:06.019
"Yeah. Like I said the other day, cats are cool. They're calm, thinking creatures but ready to pounce."

81
00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.317
"Kind of like catchers," said Patrick.

82
00:07:09.318 --> 00:07:10.739
"Exactly!"

83
00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.761
The two catchers did a fist bump.

84
00:07:13.762 --> 00:07:16.778
"Sorry about the other day," Patrick said.

85
00:07:16.779 --> 00:07:19.761
Mickey shrugged. "No problem.

86
00:07:19.762 --> 00:07:22.586
You're going to make it to the Hornets' game, aren't you?"

87
00:07:22.587 --> 00:07:28.891
"Sure." Patrick nodded. "We're going to need a good hitter. I bet Coach will start you."

88
00:07:28.892 --> 00:07:36.233
Mickey shook his head. "No way. You and Dell are true partners. It's like you read each other's minds."

89
00:07:36.234 --> 00:07:49.561
Then he waved for Patrick to follow him to the family room. "Come on. It's time to get this team pumped up for the game!"
